Sample DB Schema:

Models: User, Project, Task, Comment

Relationships:
* User has_many Projects
* User has_many Tasks through Assigned Tasks
* User has_many Comments
* Project belongs_to User
* Project has_many Tasks
* Task belongs_to Project
* Task belongs_to User through Assigned Tasks
* Task has_many Comments
* User Assigned Tasks has_many Users
* User Assigned Tasks has_many Tasks
* Comment belongs_to Task
* Comment belongs_to User

Passing criteria:
Users
1) Can see Users Projects
2) Can see Users Tasks through Assigned Tasks
3) Can see Users Comments
Projects
1) Can see who Project belongs to (User)
2) Can see Project Tasks
Tasks
1) Can see what Project the Task belongs to
2) Can see Task Comments
3) Can see Task belongs to User through Assigned Tasks
Assigned Tasks
1) Can see Users Assigned Tasks
2) Can see Task belongs to User
Comments
1) Can see Comments User
2) Can see Comments Task
